WEBVTT

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.650
That was great!

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.150
I'm amazed they paired so well.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.610
Still, we won't be able to taste this again
while we're here, will we?

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.030
That was the last of it.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.070
Yes, but there's something even better
than that anchovy soup.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.610
What? Really?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.530
The wild greens Her Majesty picks are better.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.940
Huh?

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.030
Well, they are quite good...

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.400
Wild greens?

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.570
I've eaten wild greens before...

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:53.530
...but I'm sure that your kingdom's greens,
bathed in so much light,

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.230
must taste better than any we've eaten.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.690
Let's go.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.400
Huh?

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.900
Let's all go pick wild greens!

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.650
Your Majesty,

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.980
there's no need to hurry so much.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.230
No, the earlier, the better.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.440
You look happy, Your Majesty!

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.730
Yes, of course I--

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.190
Your Majesty!

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.440
I'm fine. I just stumbled a little.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.440
Please be careful.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.650
You aren't exactly in perfect health yet.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:47.900
I know.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.480
Come on, let's all get going!

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.440
Hey, what do you want to bring along
a dangerous thing like that for?

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.360
You never know where darkness
may be lying in wait.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.440
That's a knight commander for you.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.730
You're always on your guard.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.480
"Shironeko Project ZERO CHRONICLE"

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.530
<i>Under the "light and dark" called justice</i>

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.150
<i>our wishes run aground in twilight</i>

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:56.530
<i>If you want the tomorrow</i>
<i>on the other side of the mirror,</i>

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.530
<i>go through nightmares</i>

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.440
<i>Lives fragmented like the sea and sky</i>

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.980
<i>Even if we realize that</i>
<i>their resemblance is false,</i>

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.730
<i>we can at least not give it words, give it form,</i>

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.360
<i>or doubt our bonds</i>

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:20.150
<i>and tell ourselves that</i>
<i>even blindness is a mercy</i>

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.690
<i>White or black? The scales of Libra</i>

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.480
<i>waver cruelly</i>

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:30.690
<i>Together we cling, tenaciously,</i>
<i>to our sliver of a promise</i>

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.730
<i>We looked up at a nebula</i>

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.690
<i>of numberless dystopias</i>

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:38.360
<i>I crawled through the mud, mind ablaze,</i>

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.940
<i>and met you on the far side</i>
<i>of the scales of Libra</i>

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.000
"Shironeko Project ZERO CHRONICLE"

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.960
"Chapter 7"
"Picking Wild Greens"

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.400
This way, everyone.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.650
It's huge.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:12.570
That's really something.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.780
Do you always pick greens here?

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:18.650
Yes, they grow thickly in this area.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.570
I see.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.650
All right, let's get started.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.030
Hey, since we're all here,
how about a competition?

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.150
What do you mean?

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:32.030
Just picking greens won't be much fun.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.980
Let's split into pairs and
see who can pick the most.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.690
That sounds fun!

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:43.110
This herb's name is iris;
it means "bringer of joy."

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.860
Just look at this, Your Highness!

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:48.940
You're on!

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.610
What a lovely idea!

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:51.820
How about you?

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.690
I don't mind.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.030
How will we divide up the teams?

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.280
Hmm, good question.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.150
Oh, I know.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.860
We should pair up to promote exchange
between our kingdoms, don't you think?

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.150
Huh?! Oh, yes! I agree!

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:14.070
That does seem like the best option, doesn't it?

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.980
What's got you feeling down?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.440
Exchange is all well and good,
but for security, I should go with Her--

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.070
Oh, wait, before that.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:29.940
There are some things you have to
watch out for while picking wild greens.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:35.070
Some of them are poisonous
if not prepared properly.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.150
They also have to be picked properly.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.280
Take these angelica shoots, for instance.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.860
"Angelica shoots"?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.900
They look like thorny, skinny trees to me.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.400
That's right.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.280
These trees have shoots on their tips.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.190
You take them like this and...

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.280
Got it!

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.230
Oh! You brought us some of those before!

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.940
Yes. Oh, but the shoots turn bitter
once they grow too long,

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.360
so be careful to pick ones about this size.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.530
Even bitterer than the last ones?

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:16.110
Also, if you pick all the shoots off a trunk,

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:19.570
the tree will die, so be careful.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:21.780
Oh, fuki buds!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.610
You see these?

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.940
You twist them from the roots, like this.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.400
Got it!

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.980
Wow!

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:37.530
There are also flowering ferns,
bracken, fiddleheads, chives,

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.860
and a lot of other wild greens.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:45.070
If you see something and don't know
how to pick it or if it's edible, just ask me.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:48.730
It sounds like we'd better leave
Her Majesty out of the competition.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:49.780
Sounds like it.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.820
What?!

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.030
Yes!

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.530
Okay, we've got our pairs.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.610
Let's go!

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:58.980
Sure.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.980
L-Let's do our best.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.900
Y-Yes, let's.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.900
Let's get to it, Sheama.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.610
Why are you acting so familiar all of a sudden?

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:21.150
Why not? It'll help deepen our friendship.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.110
Right?

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:29.820
I look forward to working with you, <i>Mr. Envoy</i> .

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.780
Suit yourself.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:38.070
Now then, let's all get going!

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.190
Over here.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.610
Whoa! What're these, again?

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:53.860
Her Majesty called them fuki buds,

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:58.650
but they look like they've bloomed
more than the ones she picked.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.320
What difference does that make?

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.440
Let's pick 'em and keep going!

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.360
No!

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.860
What gives?

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.860
We have to check with Her Majesty first.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.070
You sure are earnest.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:16.730
Think that's another difference
between people from our kingdoms?

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:22.320
I don't think it's anything like that.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.480
It's an issue of individual personality.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.150
That's for sure.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.570
Excuse me for earlier.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.980
Now, take these.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.360
S-Sure.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.230
Don't you want to check about them?

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:43.360
This level of difference shouldn't be an issue.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.070
Look!

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.480
Those plants look like birds' feet!

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.570
You think we can eat them?

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.230
I'm not sure.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.610
We'll have to ask.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:00.280
Oh! Your Majesty!

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:05.440
What is it?

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.190
Your Majesty, look at these!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.860
Oh my,

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.570
this is bird's foot astilbe.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.820
I knew it looked like birds' feet!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.360
Is it edible?

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:19.780
Yes, it's easy to eat boiled.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.610
Wow!

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:27.070
You can also dry the roots in the shade
to make a natural remedy.

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:30.150
It's used to treat colds.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.780
You know a lot about herbs.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.360
O-Oh, not really.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.690
These aren't too difficult.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:44.110
Pull it up from just below
the leaves and you'll be fine.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.280
Oh!

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.110
There are more!

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.900
Would you mind if I accompanied you?

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.230
No.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.280
Thank you.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.570
E-Excuse me.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:10.150
Not at all.

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:19.530
H-Hey, why is your hand on your sword hilt?!

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:24.150
I-I'm just watching to make sure that no one
from Black does anything to Her Majesty!

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:28.230
Do you think we'd do anything like that?

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.690
N-No! Excuse me.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.440
I'm not doubting you or...

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.360
I hope not.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.190
Wh-What is it?

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:53.070
You--the people of Black--seem to
trust each other a lot, like we do.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.860
That's because I realized...

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:02.400
...that he has the potential
to be our next king.

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:08.610
If abandoning and killing people
is the only way to become king,

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:12.230
then I'll find another way.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.860
I glimpsed an ideal,

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:19.150
so I have a duty to devote my life to it!

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.030
What?!

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.860
I will change this world

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.980
so that people can be happy!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:32.110
I sympathized with his words.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.530
I never imagined he was so impressive.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.190
Adel.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.610
Oh, no!

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.690
I didn't mean Adel!

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:45.400
What's up?

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:50.980
"No. 07 The Flavor of Angelica Shoots"
"Angelica shoots are sometimes called the
king of wild greens. In the Kingdom of White,
people are allowed to pick them freely.
Their exquisite flavor is difficult to put
into words. It has even been said that
bears stare at them in your hands."

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:54.320
Were you all able to pick a lot?

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.230
Yup!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:57.690
Yes.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:04.030
Oh my! So much bracken, fiddleheads,
plantain lilies, and even bird's foot astilbe!

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.730
And you picked them all so nicely!

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.940
And you have...

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.610
My, so many fuki buds!

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:25.230
Some of them have started to bloom a little,

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:29.190
but not enough to be a problem.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:30.400
That's good.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:31.900
Yes.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.530
And...

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.820
Oh, <i>koshiabura</i> .

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:42.400
But... all the rest are inedible.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.480
You should have asked me if you weren't sure.

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.570
S-Sorry.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:55.730
Well, it looks like we've got the most.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:59.030
I wonder. Let's count them up.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:02.320
It's obvious that we've got more.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:08.360
Yay! We did it!

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.190
Yeah.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.400
We lost.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.400
They definitely beat us in numbers,

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.900
although we're ahead in terms of weight.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.780
Well, we put up a good fight.
Isn't that what counts?

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.860
I-I guess so.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.820
Now we'll use the wild greens all of you picked

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.570
and the ones I picked

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.230
to cook a meal.

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:32.030
All right!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.650
What are you smiling for?

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:48.690
Her Majesty is cooking for us!

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:51.440
Of course I'm happy!

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:52.900
Oh,

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:56.320
I bet eating it all together
will make it even tastier!

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:58.860
Yeah.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:08.030
Well then, let's help get things ready.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.900
Adel, would you guys fetch some dry branches?

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.190
Huh? Sure!

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:13.860
Leave it to us!

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.570
We'll draw water.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.360
All right.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.820
If you're looking for water, I know a good spot.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.730
Let's go together.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.150
They're warm.

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:39.320
It's like all these
dead branches are still alive.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:40.480
I see.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:45.480
I suppose sunlight must be a rarity for you.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.360
Yes. A ray shines through
the clouds occasionally...

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:56.150
...but I never imagined
that it could feel so pleasant.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:00.940
Feel free to bask in as much of it
as you want while you're here.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.320
You soak them to get rid of the bitterness.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:20.110
This is how we prepare them in our kingdom.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:25.320
Wow, it comes right out.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:30.980
In our kingdom, we have to leave them
overnight or they're too bitter to eat.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:35.190
This must be another benefit of Pure Soul.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.480
It's certainly convenient.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:42.610
Oh, please go back ahead of me.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.530
I'll bring them along soon.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.980
All right. We'll get things ready.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:59.230
Hey, this should be plenty, right?

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:02.190
No, it's not nearly enough.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.480
We need at least this much,
or the fire will die right away.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.860
Theo?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.070
What's wrong?

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.190
Theo is missing?!

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.820
Now you mention it, I haven't seen him.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:25.280
Damn it, where did he run off to alone?!

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:27.980
I'll go that way!

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:29.230
You check there.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.150
Theo!

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:37.230
Hey, Theo!

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:13.650
Queen of Light!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:14.730
Huh?

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:17.610
Theo is--

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.980
Have you seen Theo?!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:47.860
If you're looking for Theo,
he already went back.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.650
He was carrying a lot of dry branches.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:17:59.940
He left with Sheama and Groza.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.360
He did?

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.730
Thank goodness.

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:08.400
I'm terribly sorry!

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:22.070
Thank you very much.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:28.320
You showed so much concern for Theo.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.030
It was nothing.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.320
Let's dry our clothes.

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:50.070
Phious!

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:51.730
Theo. So, you came back?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:57.730
Yup! You told me to go back to where I started
if I ever got separated from you.

00:18:57.730 --> 00:18:59.320
I suppose I did.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:02.070
Seriously? I was panicking.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:11.940
I'm sorry to keep you all waiting.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:13.610
Welcome back.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:21.110
I see you two got friendly.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:25.150
It's not like that.

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:26.480
Oh.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:29.940
A-After all that work,
we've got to make this delicious!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.780
I suppose we do.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:35.190
Please, let me help you cook.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.360
What?! O-Of course.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:42.230
The Queen of Light's home cooking? I can't wait!

00:19:56.860 --> 00:20:00.190
Well? How do you like our kingdom's wild greens?

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:03.070
Isn't it at least as good as
what we had the other day?

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:07.690
Definitely! This is great!

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.690
There's plenty more.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:13.820
You don't need to rush.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.860
What do you think? Was it a little bitter?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.570
No, it's delicious.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:25.730
It was a lot less bitter than
what we eat down below.

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:28.730
And it smells wonderful.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:32.400
I'm glad.

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.610
Have you tried these?

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:48.480
Delicious.

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:52.360
But if only it had a little more salt...

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:56.110
I think it's plenty tasty just like this.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:00.400
Still, it wouldn't hurt to try.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:01.650
You <i>do</i> have salt!

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.110
We can't get much, though.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.940
It's great!

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.650
It really is.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:22.030
I knew that would do the trick.

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:26.900
I suppose we'll need to sign
a trade agreement as soon as possible.

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:32.030
Are you asking me to bring
that offer home, as an envoy?

00:21:33.110 --> 00:21:36.900
But we can't decide
something like that on our own.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:43.110
And not just food and goods.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.190
I hope that

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:50.730
we'll be able to spend time with
all of you like this from now on.

00:22:16.530 --> 00:22:21.280
<i>I walk the quiet streets alone</i>

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:24.900
<i>in my memories</i>

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:28.360
<i>The times I can't see you</i>

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:34.690
<i>lead me a little astray, a fleeting light</i>

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:44.150
<i>I want to touch your darkness,</i>

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:54.360
<i>what lies beyond it and its truth</i>

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:57.900
<i>Let me light your darkness</i>

00:22:57.900 --> 00:23:00.690
<i>Even if we're apart</i>

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:07.400
<i>Won't you let me light your darkness?</i>

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:10.190
<i>I'll find you</i>

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:18.610
<i>Run, light,</i>

00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:21.940
<i>to where you are</i>

00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:24.780
<i>Through the dark</i>

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:30.110
<i>Through the dark</i>

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:46.940
"Next Time"
"Chapter 8: A Promise"
